Given differential equation is,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
x \frac{d y}{d x}-y=x^{4}-3 x \\
\Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x}-\frac{1}{x} y=x^{3}-3
\end{array}
\]<br>General differential equation of this type is given by<br>\( \frac{d y}{d x}+P(x) y=Q(x) \)<br>Here \( P=-\frac{1}{x} \) and \( Q=x^{3}-3 \) So, I.F. factor is given by,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\text { I.F. }=e^{\int P d x}=e^{\int-\frac{1}{x} d x} \\
=e^{-\log x}=e^{\log \left(\frac{1}{x}\right)}=\frac{1}{x}
\end{array}
\]

Given that, \( x^{y}=e^{x-y} \)<br>Taking log both sides, we get<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
y \log x=x-y \\
y(1+\log x)=x \\
\Rightarrow y=\frac{x}{(1+\log x)}
\end{array}
\]<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\text { So, } \frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{(1+\log x)-x\left(\frac{1}{x}\right)}{(1+\log x)^{2}} \\
=\frac{\log x}{(1+\log x)^{2}}
\end{array}
\]

Given that, \( x^{m} y^{n}=(x+y)^{m+n} \)<br>Taking log both the sides, we have<br>\( m \log x+n \log y=(m+n) \log (x+y) \)<br>Differentiating both the sides with respect to \( x \), we get<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\frac{m}{x}+\left(\frac{n}{y}\right) \frac{d y}{d x}=(m+n)\left(\frac{1+\frac{d y}{d x}}{x+y}\right) \\
\Rightarrow \frac{m}{x}-\frac{m+n}{x+y}=\left(\frac{m+n}{x+y}\right) \frac{d y}{d x}-\left(\frac{n}{y}\right) \frac{d y}{d x} \\
\Rightarrow \frac{m x+m y-m x-n x}{x(x+y)}=\left(\frac{m y+n y-n x-n y}{(x+y) y}\right) \frac{d y}{d x} \\
\Rightarrow \frac{1}{x}=\frac{1}{y} \frac{d y}{d x} \Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{y}{x}
\end{array}
\]

Given that, \( \tan ^{-1}\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)=\alpha \)<br>\( \Rightarrow x^{2}+y^{2}=\tan \alpha \)<br>Differentiating with respect to \( x \), we get<br>\[
