\beta=\frac{0.49 \mathrm{~mA}}{0.01 \mathrm{~mA}}=49
\end{array}
\]<br>Therefore, current gain \( \beta \) is \( 49 \).

Using Boolean law \( A \times A=A \), we get<br>\( \overline{A \cdot A}=\bar{A} \) and \( \overline{B \cdot B}=\bar{B} \)<br>By de Morgan's law, we have<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\bar{A} \cdot \bar{B}=\overline{\bar{A}}+\overline{\bar{B}}=A+B \\
